What it does

quartermaster keeps addon folders in sync across the machines you own. It opens
a page in a browser you are already signed in to, collects the archive links on
it, hands them to a downloader you already run, unpacks what arrives, and copies
the addon folder into a World of Warcraft install you name. A small JSON
manifest lets the other machines pick up the same files.

The engine itself is generic. What to fetch and what to call it live in
feeds/*.json, one file per feed; the ones in this repository are examples.

